## Lab: Source to Silicon on Your Board

1. Build the C blinky from section 2.1 and flash it.
2. Run `arm-none-eabi-objdump -d` on the ELF file. Find the store to `0x40020018` and match it to the C line.
3. Compile once with `-O0` and once with `-Os`. Compare the assembly of the delay loop and explain why `volatile` still matters.
4. Run `arm-none-eabi-objcopy -O ihex` and find the data record that contains the code. Decode its byte count and address fields.
5. (Optional) Use a logic analyzer or oscilloscope on PA5 and compare the measured period to your delay count.

